streaming_contracts:
Frame model (line-delimited JSON in wire):
- {"seq": 123, "type": "text"|"structured"|"tool_event", "payload": {...}, "checkpoint_hint": optional_string }
Checkpoint envelope: when server emits a checkpoint frame: {"seq": N, "type": "checkpoint", "payload": {"checkpoint_id": "abc123", "digest": "sha256:...", "schema_hints": ["draft.invoice.v1"]}}
Resume semantics: client reconnects with last_ack_seq. Server will replay frames with seq > last_ack_seq up to a replay window or send a truncation notice if checkpoint jumped. If a checkpoint_id is provided, server can fast-forward to that checkpoint and emit a compact delta.
Backpressure: SDK exposes tokenBudget and a soft-queue; server may send flow-control frames that indicate preferred client read-rate.

structured_output_examples:
Example partial invoice envelope (frame):
{
  "seq": 412,
  "type": "structured",
  "payload": {
    "schema": "draft.invoice.v1",
    "status": "partial",
    "data": {
      "line_items": [{ "desc": "Design work", "amount": 1800 }],
      "subtotal": 1800
    },
    "checkpoint_hint": "cp_2024_11_14_412"
  }
}
Final frame removes status partial and contains full data and signature.
Example tool_event frame (email send):
{
  "seq": 413,
  "type": "tool_event",
  "payload": {
    "tool": "send-email",
    "call_id": "call_987",
    "idempotency_key": "uuid-2345",
    "status": "provisional",
    "preview": {"subject": "Your invoice"}
  }
}
